id: sudden-stop
name: Sudden Stop
type: counter
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
suddenStop: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Dig in when somebody sends you flying. Cut up to half your Might off the Squares
  you are moved, halve any Collision Damage, and if nothing was hit, take a
  Movement Maneuver out of sequence.
text: >
  Sudden Stop Maneuver: By hitting the ground, stabbing your Ki into the floor,
  using your flight to suddenly stop as if you hit an invisible wall, or any other
  method, you stop your movement.
  –Maneuver Type: Counter
  –Action Cost: 1 Counter
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Effect: If you are moved by the effect of another Character, you may use this
  Maneuver to reduce the number of Squares you move by a number of Squares up to
  1/2 of your Might. Additionally, halve any Collision damage you take as a result
  of this movement and you may choose to ignore the effects of any Feature
  Qualities or Environment Qualities that affect you for Feature Collision or
  Ground Collision respectively.

  If you end this movement without Collision, you may use the Movement Maneuver as
  an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.

---

# No script. What this answers is a card - somebody else's Clash, won, with a
# movement behind it - and a script cannot reach one. `suddenStop: true` hands it to
# the code, as every Counter Maneuver that does more than pay for itself is handed.
#
# "If you are moved by the effect of another Character." In this system that is one
# shape and not several: every effect that moves somebody opens a Clash carrying a
# collision - the Launch Maneuver, the Thrust Maneuver's Push Back, the Knockback
# Advantage - and the Character moved is the Defender of it. So this is offered on
# any settled Clash whose collision is armed, to the side being thrown, before
# anybody has said what the collision cost.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - you say how many Squares to cut, up to half your Might rounded down, and the
#     card says it
#   - the collision on that card is halved from then on, whoever ends up entering a
#     number into it. Launching doubles the same number, and the two are settled
#     together as one multiplier rather than one after the other, so double-then-
#     halve comes out at what was typed rather than a point short of it
#   - the Movement Maneuver is offered out of sequence, with its condition named
#
# --- What is not built, and why -----------------------------------------------------
#
# "You may choose to ignore the effects of any Feature Qualities or Environment
# Qualities that affect you for Feature Collision or Ground Collision respectively."
#
# There are no Feature Qualities or Environment Qualities in this system, and no
# Feature Collision or Ground Collision either: what a collision costs is a number
# the table agrees on and the card takes off your Life Points. So there is nothing
# here for this to switch off. The card says you ignore them, which is the whole of
# what can honestly be done until those exist, and this is where the other half goes
# when they do.
#
# "If you end this movement without Collision." Whether anything was hit is the
# table's - the collision is a number somebody types, and not typing one is how a
# movement that hit nothing looks. So the Movement Maneuver is offered with the
# condition written on it rather than withheld until a machine can tell: an offer
# nobody may take is worse than one that says when it may be taken.
